# Article Writing Rules

## Frontmatter (REQUIRED)

Every `.md` article MUST start with YAML frontmatter:

```yaml
---
title: Human-Readable Title
description: One-line SEO description (50-160 characters)
---
```

## Document Type Compliance

Before writing or editing an article, check `ARTICLE_TAXONOMY.md` for its assigned Document Type (A–L), then follow the structure defined in `Document-Format.txt`.

| Type | Structure |
|------|-----------|
| A | Overview → How Platform Is Designed → What This Enables → Key Principles |
| B | Overview → Roles Covered → What Each Role Can Do → Access Notes |
| C | Overview → How to Navigate → What You Will See → Helpful Tips |
| D | Overview → Who Can Use → When Used → Step-by-Step → Rules → What Happens Next |
| E | Overview → Lifecycle Overview → Status Meanings → What Each Status Indicates |
| F | Overview → Possible Outcomes → What Each Means → Next Steps |
| G | Overview → Reference Details → Important Notes |
| H | Overview → Categorized Q&A → Related Articles |
| I | Overview → What Changed → Impact on Users → What To Do |
| J | Overview → What [X] Is → Key Features → How It Works |
| K | Overview → Workflow Summary → Key Stages → Roles Involved |
| L | Overview → Evaluation Criteria → Making Decisions → Outcomes |

## Content Quality Standards

- **Minimum depth:** 600+ words for process docs (D), 500+ words for reference/status docs
- **Specificity:** Use actual field names, status values, dropdown options from the codebase
- **No placeholders:** Never use TODO, TBD, "coming soon", or "[insert content]"
- **No fiction:** Only document features that exist in the code
- **Tables:** Use for status definitions, role permissions, field descriptions, comparisons
- **Cross-references:** Link related articles: `[Settlement](36_Settlement_and_NFT_Transfer.md)`

## Writing Tone

- Professional, clear, user-friendly
- Audience: Platform users (non-technical), not developers
- Explain WHY, not just WHAT
- Define any technical term on first use
- Use active voice: "Click Submit" not "The Submit button should be clicked"
